# ...but the visual baselines are a committed artefact, and the global *.png
# rule above would otherwise swallow them. They are platform-suffixed and
# Linux-only on purpose — see e2e/README.md.
!e2e/visual.spec.ts-snapshots/*.png
.playwright/
# Local artifacts from retired capacity implementations. Nothing reads these.
ai_engine/capacity_report.json
ai_engine/machine_profile.json
ai_engine/_bench/
# Disposable pytest base-temp directories used for isolated test artifacts.
.pytest-tmp-*/
ai_engine/*.engine
# Build artifacts, not sources: both are exported from epoch50.pt, which IS
# tracked. The .engine is tied to the GPU, driver and TensorRT version that
# built it and is useless anywhere else; the .onnx is an intermediate of the
# same export chain. Rebuild them per machine rather than committing 10-20 MB
# of binary that no other machine can load.
ai_engine/*.onnx
# Real accident footage, test-only, permanently. No public licence; shows identifiable
# people/vehicles/locations. Already covered by *.mp4 above; this is belt-and-suspenders
# so the rule holds even if a non-.mp4 file ever lands here.
ai_engine/eval/clips/
# MediaMTX generates a self-signed cert and EC private key for its MoQ/WebRTC
# listeners on first run, in whatever directory it is started from. The
# documented command is `mediamtx mediamtx.yml` from the repo root, so every
# developer who simulates cameras drops these here. Never commit a .key.
auto.crt
auto.key
# Kept local, deliberately not published. This repository is public.
#   Final-Paper.pdf         — the capstone paper itself, a 3.2MB binary
#   paper-edits-required.md — corrections the port makes necessary to that paper
# port-handover.md IS tracked: docs/archive/ establishes that internal
# planning and audit documents belong in this repo, and it is what lets a fresh
# session resume the work.
ai_engine/docs/Final-Paper.pdf
ai_engine/docs/paper-edits-required.md
# TLS certs (LAN demo profile) — never commit a private key
certs/
# Optional real frames for seeded snapshots (docs/archive/dev_plan/01_PKG_seed_core.md
# Step 6). Absence is fine - the seeder falls back to an embedded placeholder JPEG.
backend/app/dev/assets/snapshots/
# Claude Code: share skills with the team, keep everything else local.
# .claude/worktrees/ holds full repo checkouts and must never be committed.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.logs/
# Codex desktop configuration is machine-local and must not be committed.
/.codex/config.toml
